Android's cRSubGame holds 16 slugs where Windows holds 8: its constructor (00025a68)
builds them from +0x33a8 to +0x41a8, and AddSlug (0007953c), ReSet (0006c328),
RemoveBods (00076ba0), cRSubGoldy::Collision (00077f5c) and cRSubGolb::AI (000635d4)
walk all 16. Mobile segments fill them: Barrage has 16 slugs within 40 rows, SlugLine 9
in three. Every port build reserves 16; AddSlug fills 16 in Ultimate and 8 in Original.
Ultimate's RowFromPos clamps at 3599, the last of the rows 02-mobile-capacity reserves,
as Android's (0006c008) does; Original clamps at 3199, as Windows does.

